WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:06.952
For sixteen values and eight threads per
block, each thread in block zero copies one

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.307
value into scratch.

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:13.085
Scratch is shared memory that the threads
in the same block can access.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.170
Thread one stores two, while thread five
stores six.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.274
Each must reach the block barrier before
any thread continues.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:25.889
The barrier lets thread one read the value
written by thread five.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:32.753
At a distance of four, thread one reads
scratch at index five and adds six to its

00:00:32.753 --> 00:00:33.116
two.

00:00:33.296 --> 00:00:37.313
Find that read and the resulting write in
the selected thread trace.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.765
Remove the first barrier using the
experiment instructions.

00:00:41.945 --> 00:00:46.438
The browser reports a read before
initialization in its fixed run order.

00:00:46.618 --> 00:00:51.908
On hardware, thread scheduling can vary, so
a single successful run cannot establish

00:00:51.908 --> 00:00:54.350
that a missing barrier is safe.
